  "query_preview": "(This evening through Saturday)...\nIssued at 210 PM EDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Tonight...\n\nQuiet weather will continue through this evening with just some high \nclouds at times across portions of the area.\n\nTonight, there will be some high clouds from the west again. Winds \nwill diminish. With these conditions, expect patchy fog to form once \nagain. Short term guidance focuses the fog on the northeast forecast \narea again, but feel that, if the cirrus is thin enough west, patchy \nfog will be able to form farther west. \n\nWith the expected conditions, nudged guidance's low temperatures \ndown a bit in some areas. Lows will be mainly in the 40s.\n\nSunday through Tuesday...\n\nSubsidence to the west of a large upper low across the eastern USA \nearly followed by some upper ridging moving in will keep the weather \nquiet across central Indiana during this period. At the surface, \nhigh pressure will remain in control.\n\nSome high and mid clouds will continue across the western \nforecast area. Sunday night and Monday night, some patchy fog will \nlikely develop once again with similar conditions to tonight. \n\nTemperatures will gradually warm to above normal as the airmass \nmoderates and winds become southerly.\n\nWednesday onward...\n\nA slow moving weakening upper system will move northeast into the \ncentral USA by Friday. At the surface, an associated meandering \nsurface front will linger across the area. \n\nThe result will be rain chances across central Indiana. Questions \nremain though on the speed of the system and how much forcing will \nbe across central Indiana during any one period. Thus confidence is \nlow on the specifics of the PoPs and when the highest chances of \nrain will be. The upper system will have ingested tropical moisture, \nso depending on where the surface front sets up, locally heavy rain \nmay be possible for parts of the area by Friday.\n\nFor next weekend, guidance differs on the next larger upper trough, \nkeeping uncertainty high. Will continue with some PoPs into Saturday.\n\nAbove normal temperatures look to continue into Thursday, but \nreadings a little below normal could return Friday into Saturday \ndepending on rain coverage/sky cover/where the front ends up.",
